                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4b750e54-3a91-324c-8dbe-010ae457aea1",
                        "entry_id": "794bd80b-e22f-3d5f-b0ac-6072c97fd3c0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "a ban on singing; an interdiction to sing"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "neuter",
                            "strong"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e58bad57-64bd-4ff1-80f6-94da84731e6c",
                                "sense_id": "4b750e54-3a91-324c-8dbe-010ae457aea1",
                                "text": "“„Ghamar“, wie sie schlicht genannt wird, war die erste iranische Sängerin, die in den 20er Jahren das Tabu brach vor Männern und ohne Kopftuch zu singen. Mit ihrem ersten Konzert 1924 beendete Ghamar das damalige Gesangsverbot für Frauen im Iran, erzählt Sara Najafi.”",
                                "translation": "In the 20s, \"Qamar\" (as she is commonly called) was the first Iranian singer to break the taboo against singing in front of men and without a headscarf. With her first concert in 1924, Qamar brought the then-current ban on singing for women in Iran to an end, recounts Sara Najafi.",
                                "english": "In the 20s, \"Qamar\" (as she is commonly called) was the first Iranian singer to break the taboo against singing in front of men and without a headscarf. With her first concert in 1924, Qamar brought the then-current ban on singing for women in Iran to an end, recounts Sara Najafi."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
